&lt;h1 data-hextra-search-id="quantum-threads-hybrid-quantum-classical-ml"&gt;Quantum Threads: Hybrid Quantum-Classical ML&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nagarajpoojari404/Quantum-Threads" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="#hybrid-quantum-classical-pipeline"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="#what-makes-it-innovative"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Innovations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quantum Threads&lt;/strong&gt; is an applied quantum machine learning research and engineering project that benchmarks hybrid quantum-classical neural network architectures for fine-grained underwater animal classification across 23 marine species (&amp;gt;13,000 images in the UAD-2023 dataset).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project develops hybrid counterparts to premier classical computer vision models—&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Quantum ResNet-18&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Quantum ResNet-50&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Quantum Inception-V3&lt;/strong&gt;—incorporating Parameterized Quantum Circuits (PQCs) as high-dimensional non-linear quantum kernels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="hybrid-quantum-classical-pipeline"&gt;Hybrid Quantum-Classical Pipeline&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="hybrid-quantum-classical-pipeline"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#hybrid-quantum-classical-pipeline" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div role="img" aria-label="Diagram"&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid hx:mt-6"&gt;
flowchart LR
Input[Underwater Image 224x224x3] --&amp;gt; ClassicalCNN[Pre-trained Classical Backbone: ResNet-50 / InceptionV3]
ClassicalCNN --&amp;gt; FeatureVec[Latent Feature Vector: 512-d]
FeatureVec --&amp;gt; AngleEncoding[Quantum Angle Encoding / Feature Map]
subgraph QPU [Cloud Quantum Processing Unit / IBM Quantum]
AngleEncoding --&amp;gt; PQC[Parameterized Quantum Circuit Layer]
PQC --&amp;gt; Entanglement[CNOT Entangling Gates &amp;amp; Rotation Gates]
Entanglement --&amp;gt; Measurement[Pauli-Z Expectation Measurement]
end
Measurement --&amp;gt; ClassicalHead[Classification Head: Softmax 23 Classes]
ClassicalHead --&amp;gt; Loss[Cross-Entropy Loss]
Loss --&amp;gt;|Adjoint Differentiation / Backpropagation| Optimizer[Adam Optimizer]
Optimizer --&amp;gt;|Update Circuit Angles &amp;amp; Weights| PQC
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="what-makes-it-innovative"&gt;What Makes It Innovative?&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-makes-it-innovative"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-makes-it-innovative" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="1-parameterized-quantum-circuits-pqc-as-quantum-kernels"&gt;1. Parameterized Quantum Circuits (PQC) as Quantum Kernels&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="1-parameterized-quantum-circuits-pqc-as-quantum-kernels"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#1-parameterized-quantum-circuits-pqc-as-quantum-kernels" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;By embedding classical feature embeddings into high-dimensional Hilbert spaces using rotational gates (&lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;x&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo separator="true"&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;y&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;mo separator="true"&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msub&gt;&lt;mi&gt;R&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/msub&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt;R_x, R_y, R_z&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-base"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-strut" style="height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0077em;"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="msupsub"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.1514em;"&gt;&lt;span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0077em;margin-right:0.05em;"&gt;&lt;span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal mtight"&gt;x&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-s"&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.15em;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mpunct"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0077em;"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="msupsub"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.1514em;"&gt;&lt;span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0077em;margin-right:0.05em;"&gt;&lt;span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.0359em;"&gt;y&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-s"&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.2861em;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mpunct"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.1667em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.0077em;"&gt;R&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="msupsub"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.1514em;"&gt;&lt;span style="top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0077em;margin-right:0.05em;"&gt;&lt;span class="pstrut" style="height:2.7em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right:0.044em;"&gt;z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-s"&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="vlist-r"&gt;&lt;span class="vlist" style="height:0.15em;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;) and multi-qubit CNOT entangling layers, the quantum circuit maps non-linearly separable marine feature vectors into linearly separable quantum states.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="2-adjoint-differentiation"&gt;2. Adjoint Differentiation&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="2-adjoint-differentiation"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#2-adjoint-differentiation" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Rather than relying on parameter-shift rules that require &lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt;2N&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-base"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-strut" style="height:0.6833em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.109em;"&gt;N&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; quantum circuit executions per step (where &lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi&gt;N&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt;N&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-base"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-strut" style="height:0.6833em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.109em;"&gt;N&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; is parameter count), the system leverages reversible state-vector adjoint differentiation to compute analytical quantum gradients with constant memory and execution overhead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 data-hextra-search-id="3-distributed-cloud-qpu-orchestration"&gt;3. Distributed Cloud QPU Orchestration&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="3-distributed-cloud-qpu-orchestration"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#3-distributed-cloud-qpu-orchestration" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Distributes parallel quantum kernel evaluation batches across multiple IBM Quantum Cloud QPUs and state-vector simulators, mitigating queue latency during large-scale model training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
